    "narrative": "Our optimal lineup for July 10th centers on the favorable matchup against Avila, making **Taylor Ward** (71.46) and **Dylan Beavers** (68.38) our most potent offensive assets. **Taylor Ward** benefits from a high-run-environment park factor (+16%) and a favorable matchup against the SP, while **Dylan Beavers** offers elite stolen base potential\u2014the most critical scarcity metric for LawDog\u2014coupled with the same favorable pitching environment. **Bryce Harper** (68.39) remains a cornerstone anchor, bolstered by an elite xwOBA of 0.399 and a positive park/platoon alignment that elevates his floor. Meanwhile, **Tyler Freeman** (64.22) emerges as a sleeper strong play; despite facing a lefty, his skill-adjusted projection is significantly bolstered by the SP's weak efficiency, allowing him to outperform several regular starters.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card involves **Daulton Varsho** (54.60), who narrowly missed the cut. While **Daulton Varsho** maintains a high base projection and potential for stolen bases, his score was suppressed by a negative platoon shift against the opposing lefty and the inherent risk of his pending lineup status. He sits just outside the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold, making him the primary contingency if any of our starters are scratched. We are also monitoring a 35% rain risk for **JJ Bleday** (56.85); while his platoon edge (+14%) justifies his start, the weather window is tight. We have opted to bench **Ryan Waldschmidt** (39.71) entirely, as his sub-40 score fails to meet our minimum efficiency requirements for active game cap usage, ensuring we prioritize high-upside volume across the roster.",
